<article class="env-remark" id="02SD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02SD">Remark <span data-tag="02SD">42.23.5</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be a scheme locally of finite type over $S$. We will see later (in Lemma <a href="/tag/02SC" data-tag="02SC">42.69.3</a>) that the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X) \longrightarrow K_0(\textit{Coh}_{k + 1}(X)/\textit{Coh}_{\leq k - 1}(X))  \]
</div>
  <p> of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FDS" data-tag="0FDS">42.23.4</a> is injective. Composing with the canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  K_0(\textit{Coh}_{k + 1}(X)/\textit{Coh}_{\leq k - 1}(X)) \longrightarrow K_0(\textit{Coh}(X)/\textit{Coh}_{\leq k - 1}(X))  \]
</div>
  <p> we obtain a canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X) \longrightarrow K_0(\textit{Coh}(X)/\textit{Coh}_{\leq k - 1}(X)).  \]
</div>
  <p> We have not been able to find a statement or conjecture in the literature as to whether this map should be injective or not. It seems reasonable to expect the kernel of this map to be torsion. We will return to this question (insert future reference). </p>
</article>